{
  "answer": "Each hypothesis predicts a different predicted separation, which would exceed expected noise if the difference is significant. The reserved observation tests the new prediction, ensuring it is evaluated independently of fitting. The predicted separation is calculated as (E_A(b_new) - E_B(b_new))/sigma_new, and a discriminating result is expected if the difference exceeds the noise level.",
