{
  "answer": "The b_scale factor is computed as the square of the gradient scale (b_scale = gradient_scale^2). This quadratic relationship arises because b is the integral of q squared over time, and q scales linearly with the gradient. The mechanism involves scaling the entire effective gradient waveform by the gradient scale factor, preserving delta and Delta while adjusting the timing. A computed factor does not calibrate an experimental gradient.",
  "source_ids": ["academy-pulse", "Sinnaeve2012"],
  "status": "answer"
}

