{
  "answer": "Before interpreting a computed profile, check the analytical-limit and grid refinement to ensure the model's assumptions are met. The analytical-limit check verifies the validity of the diffusion equation and the convergence of the numerical solution. Grid refinement ensures the spatial resolution is sufficient to capture the underlying physical processes. These checks are essential to distinguish numerical artifacts from actual physical phenomena.",
